    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e5cac065_def826fd",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/DrawWriter.h",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 216,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-23T17:24:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When we pad and zero because of a new pipeline state, we always want the zero\u0027ed bytes to be preserved.  Even if the new render state appends vertices, and those vertices happen to have the same stride, we need the zeroed bytes to protect from different attribute layouts between the pipelines.\n\nIgnoring for now the case of padAndZero\u0027ing because a buffer ran out of space, when we call padAndZero because of newPipelineState or because of the end of a DrawPass, there isn\u0027t an active Appender (which we can assert). This means all of its reserved bytes will have been returned, so we don\u0027t need to add a new `takeVertexBytes` function, but should be able to just call `getVertexWriter()` with a stride of 1.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 214,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 216,
        "endChar": 53
      },
      "revId": "de511d11931f30c4232627ebc65a962bc703bf18",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "76eb588f_a2763696",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/DrawWriter.h",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
