      "author": {
        "id": 3948337
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-23T19:52:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done",
      "parentUuid": "e5cac065_def826fd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 214,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 216,
        "endChar": 53
      },
      "revId": "de511d11931f30c4232627ebc65a962bc703bf18",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b0fa878b_e8c17b1b",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/DrawWriter.h",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 348,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-23T17:24:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ideally we\u0027d only use 4*stride for the first `reserve` call after `newPipelineState`, at least for ensuring that speculative execution doesn\u0027t access any non-pipeline data in front of what\u0027s bound.\n\nIf we have to align to 4*stride to make sure that the base vertex ends up a multiple of 4, then we\u0027d want to do this after any `flush()`. I think the current code aligns to a multiple of 4 for every reserve call even if the regular stride-aligned allocation would have been contiguous.\n\nIn the situation where we have multiple batched `AnalyticBlurRenderStep::writeVertices` calls without a pipeline state change between them, we will have a series of `append(6)` calls, but each uses their own stack-allocated `Vertices` appender. The `getVertexWriter()` call with `fStride*4` for each of these will create gaps between each block of 6 vertices but we are otherwise treating it as if it were a contiguous draw.\n\nTo make sure we have enough room to padAndZero when a new pipeline state comes around later on, we can request `SkAlign4(count` from the buffer manager and use that for `fReservedCount`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 346,
        "startChar": 73,
        "endLine": 348,
        "endChar": 109
      },
      "revId": "de511d11931f30c4232627ebc65a962bc703bf18",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
