      "lineNbr": 409,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-23T17:24:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "WDYT about having BufferManager just memset all remaining bytes in a buffer when it moves it from being a current buffer to a used buffer?  As long as we request SkAlign4(count) in reserve, we\u0027ll have enough remaining bytes even when the next reserve() moves to a new buffer and we don\u0027t have to try and set bytes using a VertexWriter.\n\nAlthough, we could get at the necessary byte range to zero by using `fNextWriter`.  Its limit should have been marked at the 4*count limit so we\u0027d just zero everything left in that range.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 409,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 409,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "de511d11931f30c4232627ebc65a962bc703bf18",
